As far as the logical positivism goes (and its impact on Karl Poppers
reflections on the nature and practice of science), and with other
philosophical problems, the use of English makes me want to ram my head into
concrete until my brains spill out.

It can be done, but is very frustrating. So, I hoped to expand the tools
that I think with to see if this helps.

Thanks for the tips.

I have had several responses, all of which have presented the rules in
essentially the same way, which is a good sign.

Thanks,
tamys

